ENTRY            23624   20251218   20260826   20260826       2323
SUBENT        23624001   20251218   20260826   20260826       2323
BIB                 10         32
TITLE      Competition between mass-symmetric and asymmetric
           fission modes in 258Md produced in the 4He + 254Es
           reaction
AUTHOR     (K.Nishio,K.Hirose,H.Makii,R.Orlandi,K.R.Kean,
           K.Tsukada,A.Toyoshima,M.Asai,T.K.Sato,N.M.Chiera,
           T.Tomitsuka,K.Tokoi,R.Yanagihara,H.Suzuki, Y.Nagame,
           K.Okada,A.N.Andreyev,T.Tanaka, K.Morimoto, S.Ishizaki,
           M.Okubayashi,Y.Miyamoto,S.Tanaka, S.Takagi,Y.Aritomo,
           S.Kubono,N.Iwasa,M.Egeta, S.Sakaguchi,S.Matsunaga,
           Y.Ishibashi, K.P.Rykaczewski,R.A.Boll,J.Z.Ezold,
           L.K.Felker, J.B.Roberto)
INSTITUTE  (2JPNJAE,2JPNTIT,2JPNNII,2JPNOSA,2UK YRK,2JPNIPC,
           2JPNKYU,2JPNKNK,2JPNTOH,1USAORL)
           (2JPNJPN) Ibaraki University, Ibaraki
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,111,044609,2025)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.111.044609
SAMPLE     The target was prepared by electrodeposition of
           the 10-ng 254Es material (0.69 MBq) with a 2.0-mm
           diameter (0.00032 mg/cm2) on a 0.27m/cm2 nickel foil.
           The contamination of 253Es was determined to be 20 ppm.
           The 250Cf was produced as a granddaughter nucleus
           via 254Es -(alpha)-> 250Bk -(beta)-> 250Cf.
METHOD     Double velocity method
           (TOF,COINC)
PART-DET   (FF)
DETECTOR   (MWPC,MCPLT)
           The mass and TKE resolutions were 2.9 u and 3.6 MeV.
ANALYSIS   As the average fragment velocity does not change
           after prompt neutron emission from the fragment, the
           method gives preneutron emission fragment mass and TKE.
HISTORY    (20251212R) Data received from K.Nishio.
           (20251218C) By A.Kimura.
ENDBIB              32
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           35
